  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_0954daa92ecd",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 233,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `M_COUNT` with `S_COUNT` in `int_axis_tready[n*S_COUNT +: S_COUNT]` stride (m-iface `int_axis_tready` slice). With original `M_COUNT` stride, readiness from the granted output does not back-propagate to the correct source input index when `S_COUNT != M_COUNT`, causing `s_axis_tready` to assert on the wrong source. The downstream `axis_register` then never stores the valid input, so `m_axis_tvalid` stays 0 at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_cb1771b6727b",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 301,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `S_COUNT` with `M_COUNT` in the `s_axis_tvalid_mux` multiplexer index (`int_s_axis_tvalid[grant_encoded*M_COUNT+n]`), and `M_COUNT` with `CL_S_COUNT` in `int_axis_tready` stride (line 9120). The original line 301 used `S_COUNT` stride for a `grant_encoded` (0..S_COUNT-1) index into the per-source `int_axis_tvalid` matrix, so the arbiter's grant selected the wrong source valid bit. This breaks grant_valid qualification and stalls `m_axis_tvalid` at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_af2778ae10dd",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 233,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `M_COUNT` with `CL_M_COUNT` in `int_axis_tready[n*S_COUNT +: S_COUNT]` stride (line 9120) and with `CL_S_COUNT` in `int_s_axis_tready[m]` select (line 12403). The stride error at line 9120 misaligns readiness back-propagation per granted source, while the log2 substitution at line 12403 corrupts the single-bit `int_s_axis_tready[m]` assignment. Both prevent the input register from capturing data, leaving `m_axis_tvalid`=0 at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_503814cf2245",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 233,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `M_COUNT` with `CL_S_COUNT` in `int_axis_tready` stride (line 9120) and with `CL_M_COUNT` in `int_s_axis_tready` select (line 12403). Log2 strides are bit-widths, not element counts, so readiness and select signals index incorrectly, breaking the store path to the output register and holding `m_axis_tvalid` low at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_bcd660a781f3",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 233,
      "mechanism": "Replaces `M_COUNT` with `CL_S_COUNT` in `int_axis_tready[n*S_COUNT +: S_COUNT]` stride (line 9120). The log2 stride compresses the ready bus, so only a subset of sources receive `tready`, the input register stalls, and `m_axis_tvalid` remains 0 at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_0cffe2701cd6",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 210,
      "mechanism": "Adds `&& (!rst)` to the destination-range match in the source-side destination decode (line 210). During reset (`rst`=1) the condition is masked, but the test sequence releases reset at cycle 1. If the qualifier persists (e.g., synthesis infers a level-sensitive gate), the destination match is disabled, `drop_reg` stays asserted, `select_valid_reg` never rises, and the output register never gets a valid transaction—`m_axis_tvalid`=0 at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_35cdbadc2436",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 223,
      "mechanism": "Adds explicit synchronous reset of `drop_reg` at line 223 (`drop_reg <= 0`). Without it, `drop_reg` powers up X; the combinational `drop_next` logic (`drop_reg && …`) then stays X, `int_s_axis_tready` becomes X, the input register never captures, and `m_axis_tvalid` stays 0 at cycles 4–5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_c1a2f86ca667",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 223,
      "mechanism": "Adds explicit synchronous reset of `select_reg` at line 223 (`select_reg <= 0`). Missing reset leaves `select_reg` X; the downstream `int_axis_tvalid` shift (`<< select_reg`) becomes X, grant qualification fails, and `m_axis_tvalid` remains 0 at cycles 4–5."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The trace shows `m_axis_tvalid` stuck at 0 on cycles 4 and 5 while the testbench expects 1. The failure originates in the source-to-destination handshake: destination decode, ready back-propagation, and grant qualification. Patches that fix the `int_axis_tready` stride (line 9120) and the `s_axis_tvalid_mux` index (line 301) directly address the misrouted ready/valid signals that prevent the output register from capturing data. Reset initialization of `drop_reg`/`select_reg` (line 223) resolves X-propagation that also stalls the pipeline. The destination-decode guard (line 210) is a secondary risk if synthesis interprets the added `!rst` as a persistent disable. Candidates are ranked by how directly their cited line controls the ready/valid path that feeds `m_axis_tvalid`."
}
